    Version 1.5.1
   - UI improvements for Reshade 3.x
+
+   Version 1.6.0
+  - The sample patterns come from tables indexed by the pattern setting instead of one if block per
+    pattern. Without performance mode the compiler ran every pattern's texture fetches (15 instead of 5);
+    now it runs only the chosen one's (AMD RDNA 3: 96 -> 58 instructions, 15 -> 5 fetches; Direct3D 11
+    bytecode: 67 -> 39 instruction slots, 15 -> 5 samples). With performance mode the result is the same
+    as before (the setting is a constant there). Direct3D 9 keeps the if blocks: ps_3_0 cannot index the
+    tables in a pixel shader, so the compiler would turn each lookup into a chain of selects (73 -> 136
+    instruction slots).
  */
 
